{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/Dockerfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:15:47.944656Z","id":"0ba27f1798c526b545dac06bd145a6286f0af23c8d9d54ab2daeb3ddf29449ee","body":{"detail":"No container runtime was available when deploy/Dockerfile was written; the stages (pnpm web build, cargo build --release -p clax-fleet, Debian runtime) are unverified, as is whether the .dockerignore leaves every file the web build and clax-embedded's build script read. Build it once: docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile .","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":38},"content_hash":"0dbe9a596ae916099226fc9b36051408fdb406390f70cd607e03a2f22e47e92b"},"summary":"The image has not been built","tags":["test-coverage","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/Dockerfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:36:07.215065Z","id":"d41bf829a13df76a20214c8703e7ffec0ae4ad6da1d56fad9d15947cef131484","body":{"detail":"Both build stages start with `COPY . .`, so any change to any file in the context invalidates the pnpm install layer (line 14) and the cargo build layer (21-22), and neither uses a cache mount, so each build downloads every crate and compiles clax-fleet and its dependencies from nothing. The context is also the whole repository (apps/, plugins/, docs/ …), less what .dockerignore leaves out, so a docs edit forces a full rebuild.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":10},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"9f4ed3636286f12bdc8e03e897550aae5074b352545d49055e037000ed42d696"},"suggested_fix":"Copy web/package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml and the workspace files first and run `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` before copying the rest; use `RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/usr/local/cargo/registry --mount=type=cache,target=/src/target` (and a pnpm store cache) for the builds; widen .dockerignore to directories the image does not read (apps/, docs/, plugins/).","summary":"Every image build reinstalls the web dependencies and rebuilds the whole Rust workspace from scratch","tags":["review","review:k8s-deep","devops","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/Dockerfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:41:21.162447Z","id":"fa5e2f93c150e636534973c917104d0bb1d57a7c57401ebfa585164bea6e0c02","body":{"detail":"deploy/Dockerfile:14-15 and 20-23: each build stage runs COPY . . before RUN pnpm install / cargo build, so any change to the context invalidates those layers (https://docs.docker.com/build/cache/#how-the-build-cache-works), and no RUN uses --mount=type=cache. .dockerignore excludes only build outputs (.git, target, node_modules, bazel-*, web/dist, apps/clax_app/build, …), not apps/, docs/ or plugins/.","kind":"comment","references":"d41bf829a13df76a20214c8703e7ffec0ae4ad6da1d56fad9d15947cef131484","summary":"confirmed: COPY . . precedes both install/build steps, with no cache mounts","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"deploy/Dockerfile","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:00:21.437833Z","id":"abddf1181bf1de6c2d9a753530bd67af46058df9cea5628c35cac22afeae7216","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:347050368","summary":"deploy/Dockerfile installs web dependencies in a layer of their own and uses cache mounts for pnpm's store, cargo's registry and target; .dockerignore leaves out apps/, the Worker, demo/, design/, deploy/k8s and docs but legal/ and contract.md. The image has still not been built (record 0ba27f1798).","supersedes":"d41bf829a13df76a20214c8703e7ffec0ae4ad6da1d56fad9d15947cef131484","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:52195316-c20b-49ba-9ad3-4026c7d5a1e0"]}}
